  "text": "Recipe: Corn Veggie Cutlets\nCreator: Mrs N K Manku\nCategory: Snack\nIngredients: corn flour, carrot, spring onion, amla, green chilli, coriander leaves, other vegetables of your choice, flaxseed powder, chia seed powder, Curry Leaves Dry Chatni Powder, turmeric powder, asafoetida (hing), black pepper, garlic powder, raw mango powder (amchoor), homemade soy yogurt, mint, Amla Chatni, sunflower seeds, pumpkin seeds, raisins, berries, raw salad, mixed vegetable sabji\nCooking methods: bake, no-cook\nInstructions: DOUGH: Mix all the ingredients together. Adjust the quantity of flour and vegetables to make a tight dough. BAKE: Make balls using the dough. Shape them into boats by pressing into them with our thumb. Bake both sides for 15 mins and 10 mins, respectively, at 180 C. SERVE: Fill boat-shaped cutlets with homemade soy yogurt, mint, coriander leaves, spring onion and Amla Chatni. Sprinkle some seeds (sunflower, pumpkin), raisins, berries & flaxseed powder. Serve with some raw salad & mixed vegetable sabji.\nNotes: A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (corn flour), RAINBOW VEGGIES (carrot, spring onion, green chilli, vegetables of our choice), BERRIES (amla | Indian gooseberries), NUTS & SEEDS (flaxseed powder, chia seed powder), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
